<blockquote>
<p>I have the feeling that there must be some sort of technical term that would be used for a group of infectious agents acting in concert, rather than &quot;mixture&quot;, but I have no idea what it would be.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, I don't know, either =^.^;=</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Why did he suspect that Novosadov's behaviour was anomalous? Did the intercepted WWII message lead to a standing order to be alert for serial rapists who had any connection to Nazi Germany research facilities?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hmm, you got me thinking here, because what I wrote made less obvious sense than what I thought.<br />
You are right - the depeche did call for a similar treatment of anyone showing similar symptoms - this was after the key content from the facility was found and hauled away - I'm imagining the second even more thorough emptying and demolition was more of an afterthought when they found that the other side knows more than they expected they do - so they got data from german experiments, and I imagine it was a very headdesk moment for the Division P folks when they realised the protection the soldiers hauling the stuff away apparently wasn't adequate as well, at least one showed what were now understood as symptoms.</p>
<p>From the Foundation's side, I suspect they got somewhat lucky in that the agent in question decided to take samples to be sure. I suspect what happened is that this soldier, who they knew was one of those involved in grabbing some german research showed up in a base the Foundation had (clearly undiscovered) people in, and before they could talk to him , or haul him away for information (In my headcanon , at the time amnesiacs were a new thing, and Foundation was the first to get them - he'd have just disappeared and showed up again confused) to get at least the little bit he potentially knew, he disappeared, and was brought back in the state as the photo shows, shot, and then there was the order you mention.</p>
<p>I hope this makes at least some sense, and that I unwittingly didn't introduce a shovelful more of headbangers.</p>

